ery can be rewritten by applying various strategies to improve its performance and readability. Some potential strategies include: \n\n1. Breaking down complex queries into smaller, more manageable parts, such as using Common Table Expressions (CTEs) or derived tables.\n2. Optimizing subqueries by rewriting them as joins or using window functions.\n3. Reducing the number of joins in a query by using self-joins or correlated subqueries.\n4. Improving query performance by indexing relevant columns and optimizing join orders.\n5. Simplifying complex logic by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable parts, such as using CASE statements or conditional logic.\n\nThese strategies can help to improve the readability, maintainability, and performance of the SQL query.', 'time': 4.603706121444702}
