ar AS "year"\n                          ,curr_yr.i_brand_id\n                          ,curr_yr.i_class_id\n                          ,curr_yr.i_category_id\n                          ,curr_yr.i_manufact_id\n                          ,prev_yr.sales_cnt AS prev_yr_cnt\n                          ,curr_yr.sales_cnt AS curr_yr_cnt\n                          ,curr_yr.sales_cnt-prev_yr.sales_cnt AS sales_cnt_diff\n                          ,curr_yr.sales_amt-prev_yr.sales_amt AS sales_amt_diff\n FROM all_sales curr_yr, all_sales prev_yr\n WHERE curr_yr.i_brand_id=prev_yr.i_brand_id\n   AND curr_yr.i_class_id=prev_yr.i_class_id\n   AND curr_yr.i_category_id=prev_yr.i_category_id\n   AND curr_yr.i_manufact_id=prev_yr.i_manufact_id\n   AND curr_yr.d_year=1999\n   AND prev_yr.d_year=1999-1\n   AND prev_yr.sales_cnt > 0\n   AND CAST(curr_yr.sales_cnt AS DECIMAL(17,2))/CAST(prev_yr.sales_cnt AS DECIMAL(17,2))<0.9\n ORDER BY sales_cnt_diff,sales_amt_diff\n limit 100;\n```\n\nQuery Rewrite Suggestions:\n### Suggestion 1:\n"""Here is a summary of the provided query rewrite strategies in one paragraph:\n\nThe given SQL query can be rewritten by applying various strategies such as rewriting complex queries into simpler ones, using subqueries or joins to improve performance and readability, and optimizing database operations. The query can be broken down into smaller parts, with each part focusing on a specific aspect of the data, such as sales counts and amounts for different product categories. Additionally, the use of common table expressions (CTEs) can simplify complex queries by breaking them down into more manageable pieces."""\n\n### Suggestion 2:\n"""Here is a summary of the provided query rewrite strategies in one paragraph:\n\nThe given SQL query can be rewritten by applying various strategies such as using Common Table Expressions (CTEs) to simplify complex queries, joining tables based on multiple conditions, and utilizing aggregate functions like SUM to calculate total s